An element is empty if the field name is present and the value is empty.
For example, element "firstName" has no data in the following JSON
instance.
{
"firstName":"", "lastName":"Smith"
}

An element is missing either if it is absent (that is the name/value pair
does not occur in the message) or if the field name is present and value is
empty. For example, element "firstName" has no data in both of the
following JSON instances.
Example of empty field name present and value empty:
{
"firstName":"", "lastName":"Smith"
}
Example of absent name/value pair:
{
"lastName":"Smith"
}

An element is null if the field name is present and the value is null. For
example, element "firstName" has null in the following JSON instance.
{
"firstName":null, "lastName":"Smith"
}

